Bluetooth, AirPlay and Spotify hand the output over: the newest source to
start audio takes it (hifi_source_decide, components/hifi/core/hifi_source.c),
behind a short quiet fade (hifi_handover_quiet in hifi_main.c). The source
that loses is ended properly: Spotify pauses then ends its session,
Bluetooth gets an AVRCP pause and its link is dropped a second later
(bt_sink_let_go), so the phone stops showing the Lite as its speaker. LMS
taking over does the same to a phone (decode_phones_yield). Play, stop and
rate events from a sink that doesn't hold the output are ignored, and its
data never reaches the output buffer. The two hooks are weak references,
named with --undefined for the app only, as in 0031.

A phone's Spotify login is accepted whenever its track could start, so a
Bluetooth or AirPlay source holding the output doesn't turn it away. When
a Spotify playlist ends (CSPOT_STOP), the output is let go and the title
cleared, as for Bluetooth and AirPlay stopping. Lab images get
hifi_lab_cspot/hifi_lab_cspot_data, the Spotify sink's handlers for the
lab's "phone" stand-in (components/hifi/esp/lab_phone.c, -u lab_phone).

